A||||6||Cliff Pennock||Problems posting pictures?
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||08-20-99||02:10 AM||||Ok, I know now why some pictures do not show when you post them here. I've found out that a lot of those "free web page" sites check what page is trying to view the images ("referer"). For instance, if you try to link a picture here on tripod, tripod will send a text page instead telling you that the image is served by tripod, and they supply a link where you can actually view the image. They do this to prevent that people are using their server as an image repository. So the problem is not with my server or this Forum because <b>every</b> server other than tripod's will have this problem...<p>Anyway, I'm working on a solution right now and I'm sure you will love it once it is finished!
Z||000001||FieroGT||08-20-99||09:25 AM||||Cliff, I just wanted to give you a virtual pat on the back and let you know that this is a mighty fine servece you're doing for the Fiero population at large. The first time I came across this site some time ago, it must have been relatively new and had only about 10 posts in the entire board area. I'm sorry and ashamed to say that I originally dismissed your site for it's lack of activity. Now that I came back to take a look and saw the amount of traffic (and a surprising lack of flame wars) I must say that I am very impressed. You deserve a lot of credit for putting this together and making is all happen. I am also very impressed at the high level of maturity of the board members. I never see pissing contests of any kind, and everyone seems to get along very well. This Forum is one of the best things going for Fiero owners right now. Just wanted to publicly acknowledge you effort.<p>Thanks again, from everyone here.<p>John P.<br>'86 GT - with newfound leather!<br>'85 SE - with self-taught V6 conversion!<br>'89 Turbo Grand Prix - 1 of 751 made in '89!<br>'89 Suzuki GSX-R - Feelin' good at 14,000 RPM
